# Reference results for the MiniZinc models, one per line: name, status and – for optimisation models with a
# solution – objective value. Status is optimal, feasible (a solution, not proven optimal), solved (a solution
# to a satisfaction problem), unsat or unknown.
# Computed by HiGHS (through MiniZinc, on the original model) with a 30 s time limit, so "feasible" and
# "unknown" only mean HiGHS did not get further in that time. Then checked against the MiniZinc Challenge
# results (2010–2026): where a model is a challenge instance and a challenge solver proved an optimum, that
# optimum is here – but only once CP-SAT or SCIP had proved, or reached, the same value on the FlatZinc file
# itself. A challenge instance can be another version of the model than the one compiled here. Every unsat
# is proven by CP-SAT as well – HiGHS 1.16 also called hrc__exp2-1-4795 unsat, and it is not.
